  "createdAt": "2026-07-03T22:50:20.125Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-08-08T17:14:41.044Z",
  "handoff": "# P056 — NotificationStore foundation; P061 context and T196 next\n\nCreated at: 2026-08-08T14:50:26Z\nUpdated at: 2026-08-08T14:50:26Z\nReason: Consolidated the completed P061 domain/config context with the newer P056/T198 store-foundation work. P056 is the active notification phase and this is the canonical resume point.\n\n## Current focus\n- Feature: `F009` — 🔔 Notification System — **in-progress**.\n- Phase: `P056(F009)` — notification-02: Store, Queue, Visibility + History — **in-progress**.\n- Task: `T198` — Define NotificationStore invariants and structures — **done**. Next planned task: `T196` — Implement push, monotonic IDs and slot promotion.\n\n## What was being done\n- P061 is complete: it established the app-owned notification domain/config, including extensible sources, lifecycles/defaults, canonical drafts/actions/severity, `NotificationSystem`, `notification_history_limit`, and the thin `AppNotification → ToastSpec` projection.\n- The host, not grid-ui, owns queue, deduplication, lifecycle timers, history and action dispatch; `ToastStack` receives presentation data and opaque hint targets only.\n- T198 then created `NotificationStore` in `heca/src/notification.rs` as the sole mutable owner: canonical storage, dedup index, pending FIFO, four stable visible slots, bounded history and store-owned next-id counter.\n- `AppNotification::placement` is private, preventing consumers from moving entries between lifecycle buckets.\n- `transition_at(now, ...)` is the private mutation funnel: future operations receive caller-injected `Instant`, debug-validate representation invariants, and return `NotificationStoreUpdate::visible_projection_changed()` rather than requiring the host to infer refreshes.\n- Focused tests cover empty state, disabled history and the time/update transaction contract; 40 notification tests and workspace clippy pass.\n\n## How to resume\n1. Read this handoff and inspect `heca/src/notification.rs` around `NotificationStore`, `NotificationStoreUpdate`, `transition_at` and `assert_invariants`.\n2. Start `T196` before editing.\n3. Implement the public push path only through `transition_at(now, ...)`: allocate the store-owned monotonic id, create canonical storage/index entries, enqueue, then promote into the first vacant stable slot without moving existing visible ids.\n4. Reuse P061 contracts: a producer yields `NotificationDraft`; action remains a name-keyed `heca_view::Intent`; projection remains `project_visible_toast`; no closure, bare `WmAction`, grid-ui queue logic or consumer-side lifecycle inference.\n5. Leave expiry, dedup policy, dismissal/archive, history trimming, toast host integration/action dispatch and lifecycle wake scheduling to their dedicated planned tasks (`T194`, `T195`, `T197`, `T199`–`T202`, `T395`, P059 and P060).\n6. Add deterministic tests with caller-supplied `Instant`; run `cargo test -p heca notification`, `cargo check -p heca`, and `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features`.\n\n## Files touched\n- `heca/src/notification.rs`\n- `heca-config/src/settings.rs` (P061)\n- `config.default.toml` (P061)\n- `agent-rules.md` (session rule recording)\n\n## Blockers\nNone recorded.\n\n## Next steps\n- T196: store-owned monotonic ID allocation, push and stable-slot promotion.\n- Continue P056 in task order without exposing queue, slot, dedup or lifecycle policy to application consumers.\n- Only after store behavior is ready, proceed to the already-planned host integration and action-dispatch phases.\n\n## Recent decisions\n- `NotificationStore` alone owns mutable notification lifecycle; consumers consume a projection/update result and do not reconstruct domain state.\n- Four simultaneous cards are centralized in `MAX_VISIBLE_NOTIFICATIONS`, not scattered literals.\n- All store transitions accept caller-injected `Instant`; the store never reads the wall clock.\n- Notification actions preserve `heca_view::Intent`, not callbacks or only `WmAction`.\n- `NotificationSystem::System` falls back to the in-app ToastStack with one warning per session until P063; `None` suppresses presentation but preserves stderr/debug logging.\n- Runtime history is not persisted.\n\n## Reminder\nThis supersedes the P061 handoff. When P056 is fully resumed and its work is complete, clear this entity-scoped handoff with `handoff_clear(P056(F009))`.",
  "handoffUpdatedAt": "2026-08-08T14:52:23.016Z",
  "handoffReadAt": "",
